##comment="T2T-CHM13v2 PGx fixture for the build-refusal path. It carries BOTH kinds of evidence header_inspector reads: CHM13 contig lengths (UCSC hs1.chrom.sizes, cross-checked against NCBI GCF_009914755.1) and a ##reference= value naming chm13v2.0.fa. Either alone must be enough to detect T2T-CHM13v2, and determine_workflow must then REFUSE the file rather than analyse CHM13 coordinates as GRCh38's."
##comment="The POS values below are NOT CHM13 coordinates. They are the GRCh38 positions of the same seven PGx SNPs, copied from test_data/grch37_pgx_snps.vcf's expected-liftover list, because no verified CHM13 coordinate for these rsIDs was to hand and inventing one would put a wrong number in a test fixture. Nothing reads them: a refused file never reaches a variant reader, and every assertion this fixture supports is about the header."
